<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistani rupee ends lower, seen falling.</title>
<headline>Pakistani rupee ends lower, seen falling.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1996-12-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Pakistani rupee ended 0.08 lower in the kerb market at 42.63 to the dollar on Monday as dollar demand outstripped supply, dealers said.</p>
<p>The State (central) Bank of Pakistan rate, last changed on October 22, was 40.1200/40.3206 to the dollar. The premium on foreign exchange bearer certificates closed at 6.60 percent after opening at 6.25 percent.</p>
<p>-- Ibrahim Khan 9221-5685192</p>
